 @cosmicxion  Artifacting depend a lot on the game, as some like MGS V will be identical to no FG, while others will have the HUD glitch out at times. Not too different to how native upscaling and framegen depend on the implementation with games like RE4Re having awful FSR implementation, and others like MHW introducing a lot of ghosting with FG.

Latency was shown to be only a couple milliseconds behind Nvidia, and with dual GPU setups it actually has less latency.

Not to mention, there are still a lot of games that don't support native frame generation like Helldivers 2 but with LSFG you can easily reach 180 fps. And you have a lot of old games like Elden Ring and emulators that are locked to 60 fps and have physics issues past that.
